WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.793 --> 00:00:03.087
[dramatic music playing]

2
00:00:04.046 --> 00:00:05.464
[tires squealing]

3
00:00:07.925 --> 00:00:09.927
[suspenseful music playing]

4
00:00:17.268 --> 00:00:19.729
[cackling]

5
00:00:21.814 --> 00:00:23.190
[tires squealing]

6
00:00:32.283 --> 00:00:33.283
[gasps]

7
00:00:33.284 --> 00:00:36.245
When is a pineapple not a pineapple?

8
00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.414
When it's a grenade!

9
00:00:39.415 --> 00:00:41.124
[laughing]

10
00:00:41.125 --> 00:00:43.377
[gasping]

11
00:00:46.005 --> 00:00:48.007
[straining]

12
00:00:53.262 --> 00:00:56.222
-[tires squeal]
-[police sirens blaring]

13
00:00:56.223 --> 00:00:58.601
Now. it's a party!

14
00:01:01.896 --> 00:01:03.647
[cackling]

15
00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:06.692
[suspenseful music continues]

16
00:01:07.359 --> 00:01:08.359
[groans]

17
00:01:08.986 --> 00:01:10.196
[man in green cackling]

18
00:01:10.738 --> 00:01:11.738
[grunts]

19
00:01:19.205 --> 00:01:21.040
[dramatic music playing]

20
00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:25.252
[fighting grunts and groans]

21
00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.094
[Flass] Grenade!

22
00:01:38.599 --> 00:01:39.975
[tires squealing]

23
00:01:51.487 --> 00:01:53.196
We are losing this fight.

24
00:01:53.197 --> 00:01:55.114
Not a fight anymore. boss.

25
00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:57.117
This new guy is making it a war.

26
00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:03.123
[theme music playing]

27
00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.909
[Montoya] Where the hell is Thorne?

28
00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:44.414
Detective. this will be a lot smoother
if you’d just make my client an offer.

29
00:02:44.415 --> 00:02:46.583
Scare tactics won’t get you
where you want to go.

30
00:02:46.584 --> 00:02:47.626
This guy.

31
00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:49.961
[mysterious music playing]

32
00:02:49.962 --> 00:02:50.962
Name.

33
00:02:51.297 --> 00:02:53.007
He's running things. right?

34
00:02:53.632 --> 00:02:55.217
Workin' for Thorne?

35
00:02:55.926 --> 00:02:57.177
Or did he take over?

36
00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:02.849
-Still not hearing an offer.
-Your guy tried to murder a witness!

37
00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:05.435
Allegedly. detective. Allegedly.

38
00:03:05.436 --> 00:03:08.021
He destroyed over a million dollars
worth of property.

39
00:03:08.022 --> 00:03:09.856
I’m saying he doesn’t get an offer.

40
00:03:09.857 --> 00:03:11.274
Suits me.

41
00:03:11.275 --> 00:03:13.735
'Cause even if you made one.
I wouldn't take it.

42
00:03:13.736 --> 00:03:15.695
Okay. Looks like we're done here.

43
00:03:15.696 --> 00:03:19.032
-Whose side are you on. Gordon?
-The law’s side. Detective Flass.

44
00:03:19.033 --> 00:03:22.201
You know. the thing you’re supposed
to protect and serve.

45
00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:23.703
I'm no rat.

46
00:03:23.704 --> 00:03:26.290
You of all people should know that.

47
00:03:26.999 --> 00:03:29.626
-[grunts]
-You little piece of shit!

48
00:03:29.627 --> 00:03:32.921
-What the hell? Renee!
-Hey! Ease up. Flass. Jesus!

49
00:03:32.922 --> 00:03:34.173
Guard!

50
00:03:35.424 --> 00:03:36.507
Hey. Flass.

51
00:03:36.508 --> 00:03:39.177
Next time you talk to Mr. Thorne.

52
00:03:39.178 --> 00:03:41.430
tell him to buy you a new suit.

53
00:03:42.348 --> 00:03:44.350
[car horns honking]

54
00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:49.562
[Gordon] I’m so sorry for your loss.
Mrs. Fuller.

55
00:03:49.563 --> 00:03:52.399
Let me know if your family needs anything.

56
00:03:55.027 --> 00:03:57.278
This department needed Fuller.

57
00:03:57.279 --> 00:04:00.616
He was an honest officer.
and I don’t have many of those.

58
00:04:01.617 --> 00:04:03.618
This one's the real question mark.

59
00:04:03.619 --> 00:04:06.371
He started popping up
after Thorne’s arrest.

60
00:04:06.372 --> 00:04:10.333
Since then. gangland murders
are triple what they were last year.

61
00:04:10.334 --> 00:04:11.834
there have been two bombings.

62
00:04:11.835 --> 00:04:14.504
and we only barely interrupted
a kidnapping this week.

63
00:04:14.505 --> 00:04:17.256
One of Thorne’s lieutenants
making his own moves.

64
00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:20.385
Could be. or Thorne’s finally lost it.

65
00:04:20.386 --> 00:04:23.471
and this is his revenge on the city
for putting him on trial.

66
00:04:23.472 --> 00:04:26.015
The one guy who might know
for sure isn’t talking.

67
00:04:26.016 --> 00:04:27.850
{\an8}[Batman] Mark Desmond.

68
00:04:27.851 --> 00:04:29.560
Since Thorne’s trial.

69
00:04:29.561 --> 00:04:32.897
Desmond’s the only member of the gang
we’ve brought in alive.

70
00:04:32.898 --> 00:04:37.110
And he’d rather spend the next twenty
in Blackgate than be known as a snitch.

71
00:04:37.111 --> 00:04:39.237
[Batman] He needs someone to confide in.

72
00:04:39.238 --> 00:04:40.613
Someone he can trust.

73
00:04:40.614 --> 00:04:44.702
That leaves out just about everyone
in Gotham. Unless you have a...

74
00:04:47.579 --> 00:04:49.790
-[sighs]
-[jazz music playing]

75
00:04:53.877 --> 00:04:55.253
[jazz music continues]

76
00:04:55.254 --> 00:04:58.131
The son of a bitch is gonna
get us all killed.

77
00:04:58.132 --> 00:05:00.383
He let Rocco get gunned down like a dog!

78
00:05:00.384 --> 00:05:04.887
I don’t like Eddie anymore than you do.
but Mr. Thorne left him in charge.

79
00:05:04.888 --> 00:05:08.141
If we go against Eddie.
we go against Mr. Thorne.

80
00:05:08.142 --> 00:05:11.644
-And we owe him better than that.
-And where the hell is Mr. Thorne?

81
00:05:11.645 --> 00:05:14.522
Coney Island. Timbuktu. it don’t matter!

82
00:05:14.523 --> 00:05:16.567
Eddie’s in charge. The end.

83
00:05:17.067 --> 00:05:19.067
[henchman] I'm telling you.
we need new leadership.

84
00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:21.989
You got trouble. baby.

85
00:05:22.489 --> 00:05:25.742
The tie?
You’re the one who picked it.

86
00:05:25.743 --> 00:05:27.493
Not the tie!

87
00:05:27.494 --> 00:05:30.246
Rocco getting killed ain’t sitting right
with the gang.

88
00:05:30.247 --> 00:05:32.833
Ah. damn whiners!

89
00:05:33.709 --> 00:05:36.169
They’re getting a bigger share
of the take. ain’t they?

90
00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:40.757
Yeah. but Eddie. if Mr. Thorne
doesn’t come back soon...

91
00:05:40.758 --> 00:05:43.009
What? Think I can't handle it?

92
00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:44.969
No baby. never.

93
00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:48.514
I’m just worried is all. About you.

94
00:05:48.515 --> 00:05:52.351
But maybe talk with the boys now? For me?

95
00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:54.188
Just so I don’t worry.

96
00:05:56.565 --> 00:05:57.566
Hey. boys.

97
00:05:59.443 --> 00:06:02.028
I understand there have been
some complaints.

98
00:06:02.029 --> 00:06:04.614
Tony? Vic?

99
00:06:04.615 --> 00:06:09.285
[clears throat] Uh. yeah. We. uh...
some of us got. you know. concerns.

100
00:06:09.286 --> 00:06:10.537
You do. huh?

101
00:06:11.622 --> 00:06:12.998
Well. let’s hear ‘em.

102
00:06:13.791 --> 00:06:15.958
These jobs we been pullin’.

103
00:06:15.959 --> 00:06:18.670
they pay out good.
nobody’s saying they don’t. but...

104
00:06:19.588 --> 00:06:22.965
-they’re risky.
-No risk. no reward. Am I right?

105
00:06:22.966 --> 00:06:25.718
Maybe they're a little too risky.
you know?

106
00:06:25.719 --> 00:06:28.262
Like. maybe if we wasn’t
bracing the cops so much.

107
00:06:28.263 --> 00:06:29.640
Rocco wouldn’t be dead.

108
00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:31.266
Could be worse.

109
00:06:32.017 --> 00:06:33.851
He could be in some cell.

110
00:06:33.852 --> 00:06:37.647
getting worked over by cops
‘til he spills like a broken milk bottle.

111
00:06:37.648 --> 00:06:39.232
Rocco was no rat!

112
00:06:39.233 --> 00:06:42.653
Anybody's a rat.
you put on the right screws!

113
00:06:43.779 --> 00:06:45.656
It’s like sitting in a leaky boat.

114
00:06:47.199 --> 00:06:50.452
But you know how to fix a leaky boat.
Vicky boy?

115
00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:52.161
How's that?

116
00:06:52.162 --> 00:06:54.705
-[gunshot]
-[gasping. groaning]

117
00:06:54.706 --> 00:06:56.708
-[body thudding]
-Now...

118
00:06:57.793 --> 00:07:01.004
Anybody else got... concerns?

119
00:07:05.884 --> 00:07:07.510
Speakin' of leaks.

120
00:07:07.511 --> 00:07:11.389
I hear the badges have been visiting
my old buddy Dez at Blackgate.

121
00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:13.683
I’m gonna need to put a plug in that too.

122
00:07:13.684 --> 00:07:15.477
[tense music playing]

123
00:07:16.603 --> 00:07:19.147
-[projector whirring]
-[classical music playing]

124
00:07:19.148 --> 00:07:20.731
[man. over projector]
<i>This thing's goin' south. Johnny.</i>

125
00:07:20.732 --> 00:07:22.984
[man #2. over projector]
<i>Nah. We’re getting clear of this. see.</i>

126
00:07:22.985 --> 00:07:25.486
<i>Even if we gotta drop
a couple coppers on the way.</i>

127
00:07:25.487 --> 00:07:27.531
[gunshots]

128
00:07:29.908 --> 00:07:32.869
<i>The boss don’t like us mixing it up
with the police. Johnny!</i>

129
00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:35.538
<i>To hell with the boss.
He’d been holding back our cut.</i>

130
00:07:35.539 --> 00:07:38.375
<i>I’m gonna take my due and give him his.</i>

131
00:07:39.293 --> 00:07:41.711
-[rattling]
-[Pennyworth] The paperwork is ready.

132
00:07:41.712 --> 00:07:44.839
Your transfer from stately Wayne Manor
to Blackgate Prison

133
00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:46.966
will take place in an hour.

134
00:07:46.967 --> 00:07:50.179
I trust that the legend I prepared for you
was satisfactory.

135
00:07:52.181 --> 00:07:53.681
Master Bruce?

136
00:07:53.682 --> 00:07:55.976
[dramatic music playing]

137
00:07:56.935 --> 00:07:58.103
Where are you from?

138
00:07:58.729 --> 00:07:59.855
Detroit.

139
00:08:00.439 --> 00:08:02.023
Rap sheet?

140
00:08:02.024 --> 00:08:04.818
Robbery. Fraud. Larceny.

141
00:08:05.444 --> 00:08:08.362
<i>Looking for a situation
driving for the mob.</i>

142
00:08:08.363 --> 00:08:12.283
[dramatic music continues]

143
00:08:12.284 --> 00:08:15.661
[cell door unlocks. slides open]

144
00:08:15.662 --> 00:08:17.496
The hell is this?

145
00:08:17.497 --> 00:08:19.207
[guard] New roommate for ya. Dez.

146
00:08:19.208 --> 00:08:20.626
Name's Matches.

147
00:08:22.044 --> 00:08:23.295
Matches Malone.

148
00:08:25.047 --> 00:08:27.216
Ah. who cares?

149
00:08:33.805 --> 00:08:35.349
[low chatter]

150
00:08:38.602 --> 00:08:40.354
Get used to it.

151
00:08:48.278 --> 00:08:51.531
[tense music playing]

152
00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:03.752
[tense music continues]

153
00:09:13.136 --> 00:09:14.137
[grunts]

154
00:09:15.722 --> 00:09:17.015
[grunting]

155
00:09:21.103 --> 00:09:22.229
[growls]

156
00:09:22.854 --> 00:09:24.856
[fighting grunts and groans]

157
00:09:31.196 --> 00:09:33.823
-[pants]
-What the hell happened here?

158
00:09:33.824 --> 00:09:35.575
He scuffed my shoes.

159
00:09:35.993 --> 00:09:36.994
[chuckles]

160
00:09:37.828 --> 00:09:40.330
He scuffed your... get 'em outta here!

161
00:09:47.754 --> 00:09:49.422
[cell doors sliding closed]

162
00:09:49.423 --> 00:09:51.549
-[faucet running]
-"He scuffed my shoes."

163
00:09:51.550 --> 00:09:54.635
[chuckles] Brother. you are a caution.

164
00:09:54.636 --> 00:09:57.264
Yeah. what can I say? I like a good shine.

165
00:09:57.681 --> 00:09:58.890
Name's Dez.

166
00:09:59.558 --> 00:10:02.351
You said. "Matches." before?

167
00:10:02.352 --> 00:10:04.812
Yeah. Matches Malone.

168
00:10:04.813 --> 00:10:07.524
Sorry if I was a jerk last night.

169
00:10:08.233 --> 00:10:09.651
[dramatic music playing]

170
00:10:11.737 --> 00:10:13.237
Forget about it.

171
00:10:13.238 --> 00:10:15.407
[dramatic music continues]

172
00:10:20.746 --> 00:10:25.207
[grunts] I feel like you and me met
before. sometime. On the outside.

173
00:10:25.208 --> 00:10:27.210
Not likely. I'm new in town.

174
00:10:27.669 --> 00:10:29.754
And already in Blackgate?

175
00:10:29.755 --> 00:10:32.465
Brother. you know how to find trouble.

176
00:10:32.466 --> 00:10:34.717
[tense music playing]

177
00:10:34.718 --> 00:10:36.511
Better than trouble lookin' for me.

178
00:10:37.637 --> 00:10:38.722
What?

179
00:10:42.059 --> 00:10:43.809
Maybe we oughta drift.

180
00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:44.978
Right behind ya.

181
00:10:47.814 --> 00:10:49.816
[tense music continues]

182
00:10:58.658 --> 00:11:01.244
Nice. You got a head on you.
Matches Malone.

183
00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:04.581
[Matches] Hey. I’m not taking any bruises
I don’t buy.

184
00:11:16.134 --> 00:11:18.928
Brother. I sure got lucky
getting you for a cellie.

185
00:11:18.929 --> 00:11:21.639
-Let me tell ya.
-Me. not so much.

186
00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:23.265
Who put the target on your back?

187
00:11:23.266 --> 00:11:24.434
What target?

188
00:11:25.268 --> 00:11:27.479
Two times some guys zeroed in on you.

189
00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:29.438
You're marked.

190
00:11:29.439 --> 00:11:32.691
[chuckles]
Sure. if they got a screw loose.

191
00:11:32.692 --> 00:11:35.737
Anybody messes with me.
they answer to my boss.

192
00:11:36.655 --> 00:11:40.408
-And he runs Gotham.
-Hey. maybe I did get lucky.

193
00:11:40.409 --> 00:11:44.161
I came to Gotham looking for a situation
with whoever runs this burg.

194
00:11:44.162 --> 00:11:49.208
Yeah? Okay.
Well. maybe we can talk about... that.

195
00:11:49.209 --> 00:11:51.378
[suspenseful music playing]

196
00:11:54.589 --> 00:11:56.883
[fighting grunts and groans]

197
00:12:10.647 --> 00:12:12.523
[alarm ringing]

198
00:12:12.524 --> 00:12:14.776
[dramatic music playing]

199
00:12:20.198 --> 00:12:23.160
Get these clowns back to their cell.

200
00:12:24.202 --> 00:12:26.204
[prisoners whimpering]

201
00:12:30.667 --> 00:12:34.212
It don't make sense. These mooks know
better than to put hands on me.

202
00:12:36.047 --> 00:12:37.465
I’m protected.

203
00:12:37.466 --> 00:12:41.135
-By Rupert Thorne.
-Sure. sure. Wait. You heard of him?

204
00:12:41.136 --> 00:12:43.262
Everyone in Detroit has heard of Thorne.

205
00:12:43.263 --> 00:12:45.347
If that’s your boss. you wanna reach out.

206
00:12:45.348 --> 00:12:48.642
-Let him know what’s going on in here.
-It’s Mister Thorne.

207
00:12:48.643 --> 00:12:52.062
And you don’t reach out to Mister Thorne.
He reaches out to you.

208
00:12:52.063 --> 00:12:53.981
Well. somebody better do something.

209
00:12:53.982 --> 00:12:58.152
Sooner or later. whoever’s out to nail you
is gonna get lucky too.

210
00:12:58.153 --> 00:13:00.030
[Beckett] Quiet in there!

211
00:13:03.033 --> 00:13:04.159
Lights out!

212
00:13:04.534 --> 00:13:05.577
[lights turning off]

213
00:13:06.745 --> 00:13:08.329
[jazz music playing]

214
00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:12.709
Drink up. baby. We got two bottles
of Silver Lining right here.

215
00:13:14.794 --> 00:13:16.880
Oh. damn. here comes a rain cloud.

216
00:13:17.839 --> 00:13:19.090
Better be good.

217
00:13:19.758 --> 00:13:24.137
-This bubbly goes flat. and I will...
-[whispering]

218
00:13:28.391 --> 00:13:30.644
Not... dead?

219
00:13:31.686 --> 00:13:34.480
How the hell is he not dead?

220
00:13:34.481 --> 00:13:36.982
It's almost a week since the hit went out!

221
00:13:36.983 --> 00:13:39.902
What can I say. boss? He made a friend.

222
00:13:39.903 --> 00:13:42.154
-[screaming]
-Friend?

223
00:13:42.155 --> 00:13:45.241
-[grunting]
-Dez doesn't have friends!

224
00:13:45.242 --> 00:13:47.701
-He's got... me!
-[groaning]

225
00:13:47.702 --> 00:13:51.247
[shouting] I want him dead. you get me?!

226
00:13:51.248 --> 00:13:53.040
Dead! Dead!

227
00:13:53.041 --> 00:13:55.210
Dead!

228
00:13:57.254 --> 00:13:59.713
[sinister music playing]

229
00:13:59.714 --> 00:14:01.216
Any questions?

230
00:14:02.884 --> 00:14:04.301
[dramatic music playing]

231
00:14:04.302 --> 00:14:07.931
-[alarm ringing]
-[cell doors slide open]

232
00:14:08.765 --> 00:14:10.767
[alarm buzzes]

233
00:14:34.457 --> 00:14:36.250
[sighs] I don't get it.

234
00:14:36.251 --> 00:14:38.419
I’ve never sat in the jug this long.

235
00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:41.046
Usually. I get bailed out in a day.
Two. max.

236
00:14:41.047 --> 00:14:43.215
Somebody has you marked.

237
00:14:43.216 --> 00:14:44.967
Who’d you piss off?

238
00:14:44.968 --> 00:14:46.802
You talking to the bulls
when you shouldn’t?

239
00:14:46.803 --> 00:14:48.762
You calling me a snitch?!

240
00:14:48.763 --> 00:14:50.389
I ain’t no snitch. Matches.

241
00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:53.058
Okay. okay. Easy. I’m just saying...

242
00:14:53.059 --> 00:14:54.853
Yeah? Well. don't.

243
00:14:55.812 --> 00:14:58.063
You know what? Drift.

244
00:14:58.064 --> 00:15:00.065
I need to think.

245
00:15:00.066 --> 00:15:01.651
[Matches] Suit yourself.

246
00:15:02.819 --> 00:15:05.322
[suspenseful music playing]

247
00:15:09.534 --> 00:15:11.995
-[struggling. groaning]
-[cracking]

248
00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:14.748
[gun cocks]

249
00:15:15.332 --> 00:15:16.333
[gunshot]

250
00:15:18.043 --> 00:15:19.628
[suspenseful music continues]

251
00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:25.759
[fighting grunts and groans]

252
00:15:36.478 --> 00:15:38.479
[grunts. struggles]

253
00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:40.147
[grunts. pained groan]

254
00:15:40.148 --> 00:15:41.691
[grunts and groans continue]

255
00:15:44.194 --> 00:15:47.113
[suspenseful music swells]

256
00:15:51.826 --> 00:15:53.077
[pained groan]

257
00:15:53.078 --> 00:15:56.372
[grunts. whimpers]

258
00:15:56.373 --> 00:15:57.999
[pained grunt]

259
00:15:59.334 --> 00:16:01.211
[Beckett] Put ‘em both in the hole.

260
00:16:03.755 --> 00:16:05.757
[dramatic music playing]

261
00:16:09.594 --> 00:16:10.679
Matches?

262
00:16:11.221 --> 00:16:12.514
You over there. Matches?

263
00:16:13.223 --> 00:16:15.308
-[Matches] I'm here.
-[sighs]

264
00:16:16.226 --> 00:16:17.894
What you did in the yard...

265
00:16:19.145 --> 00:16:20.146
Thanks.

266
00:16:21.147 --> 00:16:23.775
Thank me by gettin' me a gig
once I'm out of here.

267
00:16:24.401 --> 00:16:27.737
[Dez] Thing is.
Mr. Thorne won’t take just anyone.

268
00:16:29.114 --> 00:16:31.281
You need like a skill.

269
00:16:31.282 --> 00:16:34.159
[Matches]
Bergduff heist in Jersey. Two years back.

270
00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:36.870
-That was you?
-[Matches] I was the wheelman.

271
00:16:36.871 --> 00:16:38.163
Damn.

272
00:16:38.164 --> 00:16:39.331
Big job.

273
00:16:39.332 --> 00:16:41.917
Then they tried to cheat me out of my cut.

274
00:16:41.918 --> 00:16:43.920
Got ugly. But I got my due.

275
00:16:44.671 --> 00:16:46.380
And so did they.

276
00:16:46.381 --> 00:16:48.298
[chuckling]

277
00:16:48.299 --> 00:16:51.009
You sound like this guy I know
from Chicago.

278
00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:54.138
Met him in juvie.
Became bosom buddies.

279
00:16:54.139 --> 00:16:56.141
Got into so much trouble.

280
00:16:56.975 --> 00:17:00.603
He shot up so many joints.
they started calling him "The Riddler."

281
00:17:01.354 --> 00:17:04.815
I got him in with Mr. Thorne.
and now. he's practically runnin' things.

282
00:17:04.816 --> 00:17:06.608
"The Riddler." huh?

283
00:17:06.609 --> 00:17:08.653
That sounds like a guy I need to meet.

284
00:17:09.237 --> 00:17:10.757
[Dez] Can't introduce you if I'm dead.

285
00:17:11.698 --> 00:17:13.282
You said it. Matches.

286
00:17:13.283 --> 00:17:15.367
Sooner or later.
these bastards are gonna get lucky.

287
00:17:15.368 --> 00:17:18.495
-[lock clicks]
-[Matches] You gotta get out of here. Dez.

288
00:17:18.496 --> 00:17:20.414
I'm already working on a plan.

289
00:17:20.415 --> 00:17:22.332
-I figure if we can...
-[door creaks open]

290
00:17:22.333 --> 00:17:25.336
-How the hell...
-I got skills.

291
00:17:25.879 --> 00:17:29.465
-Jeez. you sure do.
-You comin' or not?

292
00:17:29.466 --> 00:17:31.468
[dramatic music playing]

293
00:17:46.649 --> 00:17:48.066
Go!

294
00:17:48.067 --> 00:17:49.861
[suspenseful music playing]

295
00:17:52.113 --> 00:17:54.741
[rapid footsteps]

296
00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:56.493
[pants]

297
00:18:01.998 --> 00:18:04.000
[suspenseful music continues]

298
00:18:06.753 --> 00:18:09.339
[panting. groaning]

299
00:18:12.342 --> 00:18:14.176
[groans. heavy breathing]

300
00:18:14.177 --> 00:18:15.804
-[panting]
-Hurry.

301
00:18:18.848 --> 00:18:20.265
[grunt. groan]

302
00:18:20.266 --> 00:18:23.268
[heavy breathing. pained groan]

303
00:18:23.269 --> 00:18:25.604
[panting. whimpering]

304
00:18:25.605 --> 00:18:27.940
[alarm blaring]

305
00:18:27.941 --> 00:18:29.943
[pained groaning. thud]

306
00:18:32.278 --> 00:18:35.365
[engine revving]

307
00:18:38.701 --> 00:18:40.702
Take that. ya damned screws!

308
00:18:40.703 --> 00:18:43.247
Who’s top of the world now?

309
00:18:43.248 --> 00:18:45.457
Okay. I held up my end.

310
00:18:45.458 --> 00:18:46.959
What about your friends?

311
00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:49.003
Sure. buddy. sure.

312
00:18:49.462 --> 00:18:51.965
A wheelman like you is gonna fit right in.

313
00:18:53.091 --> 00:18:55.093
[dramatic music playing]

314
00:18:59.514 --> 00:19:02.224
Beats the hell out of
those prison monkey-suits.

315
00:19:02.225 --> 00:19:03.684
And they fit.

316
00:19:03.685 --> 00:19:05.811
Thorne controls these warehouses.

317
00:19:05.812 --> 00:19:08.898
Always need some new gear
if a job gets bloody.

318
00:19:09.732 --> 00:19:11.400
And here's Eddie now.

319
00:19:11.401 --> 00:19:13.778
[tense music playing]

320
00:19:17.615 --> 00:19:19.867
[low chuckle]

321
00:19:19.868 --> 00:19:21.159
Eddie!

322
00:19:21.160 --> 00:19:23.996
I was blissfully listening to the radio

323
00:19:23.997 --> 00:19:27.332
when some yutz breaks in
on my favorite program.

324
00:19:27.333 --> 00:19:30.002
talking about an escape from Blackgate.

325
00:19:30.003 --> 00:19:35.091
So I ask myself. who would have the brass
to even try to slide outta Blackgate?

326
00:19:36.009 --> 00:19:38.427
Then it hits me. Dez.

327
00:19:38.428 --> 00:19:39.720
Who else?

328
00:19:39.721 --> 00:19:41.471
I had to blow out of there. Eddie.

329
00:19:41.472 --> 00:19:43.056
Some guys tried to ice me and...

330
00:19:43.057 --> 00:19:44.057
Ice you?

331
00:19:44.851 --> 00:19:47.144
Who in the world would want
to ice you. Dez?

332
00:19:47.145 --> 00:19:48.645
You’re salt of the earth.

333
00:19:48.646 --> 00:19:51.815
We gotta tell Mr. Thorne
people ain’t following the rules.

334
00:19:51.816 --> 00:19:53.985
Yeah. sure.

335
00:19:55.236 --> 00:19:58.740
Thing is. he’s still... on sabbatical.

336
00:19:59.282 --> 00:20:00.700
I’m running things.

337
00:20:01.618 --> 00:20:02.868
Who's this?

338
00:20:02.869 --> 00:20:04.953
Matches. He’s a pal.

339
00:20:04.954 --> 00:20:07.205
Got me outta the jug.
I can vouch for him.

340
00:20:07.206 --> 00:20:09.208
Oh. you can?

341
00:20:09.834 --> 00:20:11.044
Matches. huh?

342
00:20:12.003 --> 00:20:14.171
You some kind of a breakout king. Matches?

343
00:20:14.172 --> 00:20:15.130
Not a king.

344
00:20:15.131 --> 00:20:16.840
-Just a wheelman who’s looking for a...
-[gun cocks]

345
00:20:16.841 --> 00:20:18.092
-[gunshot]
-[groans]

346
00:20:19.344 --> 00:20:21.429
Matches. Stupid name.

347
00:20:23.389 --> 00:20:25.891
You still got good timing. Dez.

348
00:20:25.892 --> 00:20:27.685
Just about to go on a spree.

349
00:20:28.353 --> 00:20:31.063
Eddie’s getting me a new necklace.

350
00:20:31.064 --> 00:20:32.731
Vic took the night off.

351
00:20:32.732 --> 00:20:34.901
and we could use another set of hands.

352
00:20:35.401 --> 00:20:36.653
You in?

353
00:20:38.112 --> 00:20:40.280
Yeah. Eddie. Sure.

354
00:20:40.281 --> 00:20:41.657
You bet.

355
00:20:41.658 --> 00:20:43.785
[dramatic music playing]

356
00:20:48.498 --> 00:20:50.666
[water bubbling]

357
00:20:50.667 --> 00:20:52.919
[dramatic music swells]

358
00:20:54.379 --> 00:20:55.797
Pennyworth. it's me.

359
00:20:56.464 --> 00:20:58.548
I need the car.

360
00:20:58.549 --> 00:20:59.968
[glass breaking]

361
00:21:03.096 --> 00:21:05.098
[suspenseful music playing]

362
00:21:07.392 --> 00:21:08.934
This won't take long.

363
00:21:08.935 --> 00:21:10.144
[kisses]

364
00:21:12.355 --> 00:21:15.400
What's baby in the mood for tonight?

365
00:21:18.653 --> 00:21:20.655
-[suspenseful music swells]
-[glass shattering]

366
00:21:21.781 --> 00:21:22.824
[glass shatters]

367
00:21:25.201 --> 00:21:26.995
-[whooshing. clanging]
-[pained groan]

368
00:21:28.121 --> 00:21:29.871
[glass shatters]

369
00:21:29.872 --> 00:21:30.998
[smoke hissing]

370
00:21:30.999 --> 00:21:33.041
-[whooshing. snaps]
-[gasping]

371
00:21:33.042 --> 00:21:35.378
[fighting grunts and groans]

372
00:21:36.462 --> 00:21:37.462
[grunts]

373
00:21:39.215 --> 00:21:41.634
-[whooshing]
-[pained groan] Dammit!

374
00:21:42.176 --> 00:21:43.468
[grunts]

375
00:21:43.469 --> 00:21:45.346
[suspenseful music continues]

376
00:21:45.763 --> 00:21:47.472
This stinks!

377
00:21:47.473 --> 00:21:50.183
Four times. I try to ice you in the jug.

378
00:21:50.184 --> 00:21:51.852
Four times. you skate!

379
00:21:51.853 --> 00:21:53.103
Eddie?

380
00:21:53.104 --> 00:21:56.314
Then you bust out
with your new tag-along-buddy.

381
00:21:56.315 --> 00:21:59.527
and the Batman just magically
shows up on the spot?

382
00:22:00.236 --> 00:22:02.363
Somebody squealed!

383
00:22:02.905 --> 00:22:06.825
You know what happens to squealers.
don’t you. Dez?

384
00:22:06.826 --> 00:22:08.160
No.

385
00:22:08.161 --> 00:22:09.579
I ain’t no squealer!

386
00:22:10.288 --> 00:22:11.414
Not anymore.

387
00:22:11.831 --> 00:22:14.584
-[rapid gunfire]
-[pained groans]

388
00:22:17.378 --> 00:22:18.628
[grunts]

389
00:22:18.629 --> 00:22:19.839
[car engine starts]

390
00:22:20.631 --> 00:22:23.300
-[tires squeal]
-[Dez groaning]

391
00:22:23.301 --> 00:22:25.636
[dramatic music playing]

392
00:22:30.224 --> 00:22:33.019
[pained breathing]

393
00:22:34.520 --> 00:22:36.939
[dramatic music continues]

394
00:22:38.066 --> 00:22:39.692
[Dez] Matches?

395
00:22:40.610 --> 00:22:42.028
[pained] That you?

396
00:22:44.489 --> 00:22:47.074
[pained chuckle] Of course it is.

397
00:22:47.075 --> 00:22:48.951
You're the Batman.

398
00:22:50.578 --> 00:22:52.997
Funny. huh. [coughing]

399
00:22:53.706 --> 00:22:56.750
Me and Eddie go back so far. but...

400
00:22:56.751 --> 00:22:59.961
turns out my best friend in the world...

401
00:22:59.962 --> 00:23:02.673
was the goddamn Batman.

402
00:23:04.217 --> 00:23:06.718
[long sighs]

403
00:23:06.719 --> 00:23:08.763
[dramatic music continues]

404
00:23:19.732 --> 00:23:22.485
[suspenseful music playing]

405
00:23:32.411 --> 00:23:34.079
[dramatic music playing]

406
00:23:34.080 --> 00:23:37.374
His name is Edward Nygma.
AKA The Riddler.

407
00:23:37.375 --> 00:23:40.585
Impulsive. Reckless. Highly unpredictable.

408
00:23:40.586 --> 00:23:43.672
His kind of chaos can spin out of control.

409
00:23:43.673 --> 00:23:45.340
It pains me to say this.

410
00:23:45.341 --> 00:23:49.845
but your job might become simpler
when Thorne returns to the helm.

411
00:23:49.846 --> 00:23:53.390
At least we know the identity
of the man who has replaced him.

412
00:23:53.391 --> 00:23:56.352
And he’d be behind bars if Matches...

413
00:23:57.395 --> 00:23:59.814
if I hadn’t hesitated.

414
00:24:00.523 --> 00:24:04.819
Some have said that empathy
is the sign of a healthy mind.

415
00:24:09.073 --> 00:24:11.075
Will that be all. sir?

416
00:24:14.370 --> 00:24:16.038
Very good. sir.

417
00:24:29.510 --> 00:24:31.512
[credits music playing]
